cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SDMR, please cite the archived release associated with the manuscript."
title: "SDMR: sealed ecological identification for occurrence-only species distribution models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "ZHANG"
    given-names: "RUIQI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zuizui0223/sdmr"
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0.dev0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
abstract: >-
  SDMR implements prospective information barriers, occurrence-only model
  evaluation, known-truth ecological process recovery, falsification-first
  process certificates, observation-process separation, deterministic
  scientific execution and frozen empirical confirmation workflows for species
  distribution modelling. The manuscript release preserves the completed
  Product-A v2.8.4 endpoint and reporting-only Nature Ecology & Evolution
  synthesis without authorizing additional Product-A experiments.
keywords:
  - species distribution models
  - ecological niche models
  - ecological identification
  - occurrence-only data
  - model selection
  - falsification
  - reproducibility